# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# Why this file exists: on 2026-08-10 `git status` showed 37 modified files.
# Thirty-five of them were pure CRLF churn — ~12,000 phantom line changes with
# zero content difference — masking the two files that had actually changed.
# An editor or tool had rewritten the tree with CRLF; the committed blobs are
# LF. Without normalisation every such rewrite buries the real diff, and a
# review that cannot see the change cannot catch anything.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git decides what is text, stores it LF, and checks
# it out LF on every platform. This site is static files served over HTTP —
# nothing here needs CRLF, and the CI guard parses these files directly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
